  "coverage": [
    "Native quadratic/cubic barycentric evaluation consumes resident points and bit-reversed base-field coset prefixes. Independent CPU polynomial coefficients and Horner evaluations match every claimed value.",
    "Evaluation comparisons include one-row constants, shifts 1/7/13, duplicate and base-field points, 32-point batches, 131072-row prefixes crossing the 65536-row tile boundary, and constrained 64 KiB managed memory with a 16 KiB allocation ceiling.",
    "Private point copies remain unchanged when caller buffers are overwritten. Before final claimed-value reads, evaluation transfers only one public domain-status word; native transcript samples feed evaluation without host challenge readback.",
    "Column-compressed reductions match independent CPU polynomial quotient combinations for both field extensions, differing prefix heights, multiple matrices/points, duplicate points, zero/one/general alpha and nonzero initial alpha offsets. Private alpha copies survive caller-buffer reuse.",
    "The reduction output retains the true coset shift and bit-reversed order. Alpha powers advance in original point/matrix order. One-row constant polynomials reduce to zero.",
    "A 65-column, 2048-row full-width LDE would need 1064960 bytes. Reduction succeeds under 256 KiB managed memory and a 128 KiB allocation ceiling, with a tiled denominator pass and independently audited resident output.",
    "Separate compression/transform/reduction peaks and allocation counts are admitted before work. Host checks cover invalid shapes and arithmetic overflow; device checks cover late memory pressure, empty/oversized accumulators, alpha cursor overflow and points on the prefix or expanded coset. Failed appends consume and drop the entire accumulator without publishing partial output.",
    "Scoped hidden-commitment opening consumers match polynomials derived from independent upstream CPU hiding-PCS commitments. Preflight rejection preserves RNG streams; invalid points, failed consumers and unwinds retire every participating family. Scratch is released in success and failure cases.",
    "All 103 native tests pass. Compute Sanitizer reports zero memory/leak, race or synchronization errors across 102 native tests; the intentional missing-kernel API error runs separately. Challenger and proof-RNG adapters pass all three tools.",
    "The CUDA stream feature passes 12 opening/reduction tests and two hidden-commitment integration tests. CPU/OpenCL and standalone CUDA checks, relevant OpenCL device regressions, Apple Metal cross-compilation and source-completeness tests pass. New kernels compile for compute_70 and compute_120."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This qualifies native opening/reduction primitives and hidden-prefix integration, not complete native CUDA PCS or proving. FRI folding/commitments/queries, final polynomials, full PCS orchestration, other remaining proof stages, backend selection and worker/pool integration remain incomplete.",
    "The default backend, proof format, verifier rules and security parameters remain unchanged. No native opening-stage speedup, complete-proof performance or transaction throughput is claimed.",
    "Denominators are inverted individually on CUDA. GPU batch inversion and denominator reuse remain optimization candidates to measure after correctness integration.",
    "Hardware execution is qualified only on the desktop RTX 5080. Volta compilation and Apple Metal cross-compilation do not qualify V100 or Metal execution."
  ],
  "qualification_note": "The final source was frozen, rebuilt and qualified against all 761 source hashes, which match staged Git blobs. Development build 02 reported test-harness type/API errors; these were corrected before qualification. Earlier development and failure logs are preserved. The ordinary build/GPU checks use 3 GiB host caps, and the stream build uses a 6 GiB cap with one build job. Services prohibit swap and limit CPU use to four threads. The four opt-in primitive benchmarks are explicitly excluded from the correctness/sanitizer run.",
